#
# Conformance case: transaction/concurrent-view-serializable.
#
# A logic:ConcurrentComposition whose two legs stand in a READ dependency: the
# left leg writes a situation (sitA) that the right leg reads (its precondition,
# obtaining at the shared start so the leg is independently executable). Over the
# deterministic index-order interleaving the right leg's read observes the left
# leg's write, so the engine DERIVES a logic:readsFrom edge (right reads from
# left) and a logic:happensBefore edge (left before right) alongside the single
# acyclic logic:precedes conflict. The witnessed schedule is view-equivalent to
# the serial order left-then-right, so the history logic:satisfiesCriterion BOTH
# logic:ConflictSerializability and logic:ViewSerializability — the view surface
# of the conflict-serializability contract. (For two transactions the two
# criteria coincide; the read-from / happens-before edges are the witnessed-
# schedule structure the classification rests on.)
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/transaction/concurrent-view-serializable/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .

# The compile-time reasoning contract selects the Evolution facet that classifies this
# transaction program. logic:TransactionPathEvolution drives certification to the
# transaction-path decidability class (conflict-/view-serializability; PTIME
# classification, not search).
ex:TransactionContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:evolution logic:TransactionPathEvolution .
